anomalies.fix:
In src/tenders/types.ts, make daysUntil compare pure calendar-day numbers — read the target's date in UTC (matching the stored midnight-UTC) and today's date in local time:

export function daysUntil(dateIso: string): number {
  const target = new Date(dateIso);
  const now = new Date();
  const targetDay = Date.UTC(target.getUTCFullYear(), target.getUTCMonth(), target.getUTCDate());
  const todayDay = Date.UTC(now.getFullYear(), now.getMonth(), now.getDate());
  return Math.round((targetDay - todayDay) / 86_400_000);
}

Optionally add { timeZone: 'UTC' } to toLocaleDateString in formatDate (types.ts:644), which has the same one-day display skew in UTC−X timezones.
